  Final report:
    Everything is verified and working. Here's the report.
    
    ## What was built
    
    **Content modeling** (all via the `umbraco` MCP server):
    - **Element types** in `Blocks/`: `heroBlock` (heading, subheading, image), `richTextBlock` (richtext), `imageBlock` (image, caption, alt text), `quoteBlock` (quote, attribution), `postListBlock` (heading) — each rendered through the required pipeline: block adapter partial in `Views/Partials/blockgrid/Components/<alias>.cshtml` → plain view model → ViewComponent in `ViewComponents/` with its view under `Views/Shared/Components/`.
    - **Composition** `pageSeo` in `Compositions/` (metaTitle, metaDescription) — meta only, composed onto both page types per rule 1.
    - **Pages**: `blogSite` (default template, allows `blogPost` children) and `blogPost` (excerpt, post date, blocks). `siteRoot` updated to allow `blogSite`.
    - **Data type**: custom `Blog Block Grid` (Umbraco.BlockGrid, 12 columns, all five blocks) — created at root, auto-filed by `DataTypeSavedHandler`.
    - **Templates**: `blogSiteTemplate` and `blogPostTemplate`.
    
    **Content** (all via the `umbraco-editor` MCP server):
    - Media folder `Blog` with five Unsplash photos imported from `unsplash/` via `create-media` (filePath source).
    - **The MCP Blog** — site page under WWW with hero (network image), intro rich text, and a post-list block; published and given domain `/` so it answers on the site root.
    - Two published posts, built entirely from block-grid blocks (hero + rich text + image-with-credited-caption + quote): **"What Is MCP and Why It Is Awesome"** and **"MCP in Practice: Five Reasons Agents Love It"**.
    
    **Views** (step 3, written after content was confirmed): two page templates using `Html.GetBlockGridHtmlAsync(Model, "blocks")`, five adapter partials, five ViewComponents, and plain models in `Models/Blocks/`. Tailwind built to `wwwroot/dist/site.css` via the Frontend project.
    
    ## How to view it
    
    Umbraco is running at **http://localhost:41576** — front page on `/`, posts on `/what-is-mcp-and-why-it-is-awesome/` and `/mcp-in-practice-five-reasons-agents-love-it/`. Restart with `cd Umbraco.Bench.Umbraco && dotnet run` if stopped.
    
    ## Verified
    
    - Front page returns 200 with hero, intro, and both posts listed (the `postListBlock` queries real `blogPost` children).
    - Both posts render 200 with hero, rich text, quote, date, and image blocks.
    - Image crop URLs are signed `GetCropUrl` links and return 200.
    - uSync exported the new schema automatically.
    
    ## Notes
    
    - Two compile iterations were needed on the views: `PostDate` turned out non-nullable and rich text values are `IHtmlEncodedString` — both fixed; final build succeeds clean.
    - One environment quirk, not a defect: `put-document-domains` and `update-document-type` return no output on success (verified by reading back the rendered site).
    - Nothing is broken. The site did not need any migration plans or hand-written uSync edits, per the rules.

